// Windows installer for the Minecraft Dungeons II keyboard controller mod.
//
// One exe with the mod inside (build/payload.h, generated by build.sh). It finds
// the game through Steam's library folders (or XboxGames, for the Minecraft
// Launcher and Xbox app), copies xinput1_4.dll, default.txt
// and the offline key layout editor into Dungeons\Binaries\Win64, and can
// uninstall, switch between the Default, Recommended (author.txt) and your own
// layout, open the editor, load a layout the editor saved, or open the
// settings file. Windows loads xinput1_4.dll from the game folder first, so no
// registry change is needed (that is only for Wine; see mac/wasdmod.sh).
//
// Command line (also used by the tests under Wine):
//   /find                 print the game folder it finds
//   /status  "<folder>"   print what is installed there
//   /install "<folder>"   install without the window
//   /uninstall "<folder>" uninstall without the window (keeps saved layouts)
//   /default, /recommended, /own "<folder>"   switch the key layout
//   /off, /on "<folder>"  turn the mod off (the game starts without it) or back on
//   /recordon, /recordoff, /report "<folder>"   Record Logs, and the report file
//   /serve "<folder>"     run the key layout editor's server and print its address
